{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1302191-demons-of-isidoros","id":1302191,"title":"Demons of Isidoros","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-03T07:04:21-07:00","id":1302191,"title":"Demons of Isidoros","content":"Is there much known of his various souls or first-circle demons that eventually derive from him?<br /> <br /> Or anyone have good homebrew about such things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:32:07-07:00","id":1302201,"title":"","content":"Compass: Malfeas gives us Ferand, the Chariot of Embers, his seventh soul (pp. 119-120), Hrotsvitha, the Sprawling Forest, his ninth soul (pp.107-108), and Kashta, his eighteenth soul (pp. 32-33). No official second or first circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:38:16-07:00","id":1302203,"title":"","content":"The only one I'm aware of is Ferand, the Chariot of Embers. He's a third circle demon who is either an unstoppable warrior or a chariot, charioteer and horse team fused into one entity. He spreads hellish flame for hundreds of yards around his path, but it doesn't burn those who flee or surrender - he's only interested in those posing a challenge or getting in his way. He has a firebird familiar that sometimes appears to rulers ousted from their thrones, and offers guidance and blessings to help them reclaim their land - but if they ever succeed, Ferand is released into the world. <br /> <br /> I believe he's in Compass of Celestial Directions - Malfeas. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure he's the only demon of Isidoros mentioned in 2nd ed. Maybe someone with better 1st ed knowledge knows about more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:40:13-07:00","id":1302205,"title":"","content":"Huh, ninja'd. I didn't know those last two were Isidoros'. Guess I never looked into them that closely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T06:14:54-07:00","id":1302532,"title":"","content":"Anyone run across some interesting homebrews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T09:08:09-07:00","id":1302577,"title":"","content":"Back on the old forums, Dean Shomshak (a freelancer for the line at the time) posted a preview of some Isidoros-derived demons that were <i>supposedly</i> slated for Ink Monkeys. I don't recall their names, but they were all the souls and progeny of Kashta.<br /> <br /> First, there was a Second Circle who manifested as an empty armour wrapped in serpents and riding a lion. He spoke through the mouths of his animals, and would serve as a general in battle in return for children's teeth and casks of brandy. His progeny were the Infernal Destriers, great serpents with lion masks of bronze for faces. These could transform into more mundane steeds while in Creation (though their disguises would crack under the flash of lightning), and were naturally inclined to isolate their riders and drive them to act as knight-errants and drifters.<br /> <br /> The other Second Circle was a goat-headed man with a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hata-jirushi\" target=\"_blank\"><i>hata-jirushi</i></a>on his back. He had knowledge of all glyphs of Old Realm, including a few only known to him, and his speech would be written out in burning Old Realm in the air. He was notable for sometimes passing children through the flames of his unique glyphs, thus becoming their godfather. His own progeny were the Aelchinn, warthog-headed warriors with pools of bronze ink for eyes. Armed with strange pole weapons that grew spikes and tines to represent their rank, their natural role was as drill sergeants and unit commanders.<br /> <br /> This was all years ago, so there are probably other details I've forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:23:17-07:00","id":1302790,"title":"","content":"Doubel Post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0